From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:54:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] J714s release 10: kernel v272-19 and firmware j714s16

Re-pinned from betizzel/omarchy-m5:
- linux-aurora 7.3.0.aurora17.v272-19 (7ddee362..., 44635498 bytes) from
  731670d: aurora-silicon/linux main 0c1f7e707784 plus
  patches/j714s-27.2/linux 0001-0011 (re-pinned; this week's T6050 sleep
  series, DP pin D, upstream camera tuning #2233). CONFIG_APPLE_SOC_SLEEP
  stays off. Built on the build host (x86_64 cross, clang 23.1.5, Rust
  1.98.1). The qualification pins follow 7.3.0-17.v272-19-ARCH.
- omarchy-aurora-firmware 20261014.j714s16 (2c4d90d5..., 55182 bytes) from
  a7a463a: no VRR drop-in (VRR crashed the K114s DCP,
  betizzel/omarchy-m5#25); no own aurora_drv_video.so, which
  libva-v4l2_request-avd 1.3.r11.r169.gc653eaa-2 now ships (it depends on
  that version, betizzel/omarchy-m5#34).
Nothing else changes. Set j714s-dev-runtime-07717f8c82db.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
